From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spec decode: one batch in flight with pipeline parallelism

Without async scheduling, which HPU disables for both features, vLLM keeps
pipeline_parallel_size batches in flight with pipeline parallelism. The
engine's batch queue then stores a step's drafts before it processes that
step's output, so the next step is scheduled with the drafts but without
the sampled token they follow, and the drafter gets fewer slots than rows.
Fetching the drafts also waits for each step, so the queue gives no
overlap. With speculative decoding and pipeline parallelism keep one batch
in flight, which makes the engine process each output before the drafts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
